S10-191,S10,Statistics Canada (2014). The Canadian Consumer Price Index Reference Paper (62-553-X2014001),https://www150.statcan.gc.ca/n1/pub/62-553-x/62-553-x2014001-eng.pdf,Open Government Licence - Canada,"and 15.88. 78. ILO et al. (2004), paragraph 1.26. 0: , t Lo A I 0: 1 , t Lo A I − 1: , t t Lo A I − The Canadian Consumer Price Index Reference Paper 40 62-553-X Statistics Canada 6.32 The transitive property of the Lowe formula also enables index compilers to calculate long-term price change by chaining together short-term price indices. For example, a Lowe index comparing prices in period t to prices in the price reference period 0 is obtained by multiplying the Lowe index comparing period t to period t-1 by the Lowe index comparing period t-1 with the price reference period 0 (6.10). The product of monthly chained indices provides identical results to an index that directly compares prices in period t to prices in the price reference period 0."
